  "topic": "Feature flags and remote config",
  "tag": "RELEASES",
  "script": {
    "hook": "A bad release is live, and the fix needs a week of app review.",
    "question": "Design feature flags and remote config.",
    "trap": "The trap: hardcode a boolean and ship a new build. Users stay on old versions for weeks, and you cannot turn anything off.",
    "steps": [
      "Fetch and cache. Fetch config on launch and on foreground, cache it on disk, and ship safe defaults inside the app.",
      "Stable bucketing. Hash the user id with the flag name, so each person gets the same answer every time.",
      "Gradual rollout. Go one percent, then ten, then everyone, and watch crashes at every stage.",
      "Kill switch. Every risky feature gets a flag the server can flip, with a safe fallback if config never arrives."
    ],
    "takeaway": "Ship dark, ramp slowly, and always keep a kill switch.",
    "teaser": "Tomorrow: app startup time.",
    "cta": "Comment M S D for the free cheatsheet."
  },
